This file is a deliberately conservative default — it doesn't grant any
rights away that weren't explicitly asked for. If this repository is ever
made public or shared, and you want others to actually be able to use it,
replace this file with a real open-source license. Two common, simple
choices:

- MIT — maximally permissive, almost no restrictions. Good default if you
  just want people to be able to use and modify the code freely.
- Apache 2.0 — similar to MIT, but with an explicit patent grant. Common
  choice for anything that might touch patents.

Either can be dropped in directly from https://choosealicense.com — pick
one, replace this file's contents, and update the `license` field in each
package.json if you want it reflected there too.
